  "visualBrief": "Complete individual historic principal Lambeth Palace exterior: warm-stone Blore residential range with projecting entrance and paired polygonal turrets, red-brick western towers and Great Hall, chapel and returned cloister ranges, the integral separately mapped Morton twin gatehouse, and the low eastern court-edge range. Preserve the small cloister court, open main forecourt, recessed closed main and side gates, and closed window glazing. Original simplified trim; copied heraldry, sculpture, inscriptions and interiors are excluded. Garden Museum/church, detached modern library, shared church-side link, gardens and independent cottages remain native context.",
